  "$comment": "The deterministic crisis check (docs/ai-layer.md, Safety and abuse, gate 1): it runs first on every free-text box, scripted or live, online or offline, before any length gate, parser, classifier or comic fallback. A match shows the group's sincere lines and the group's resources, never a kit and never a joke. Input is normalised (NFKC, accents and zero-width characters removed, look-alike and leet characters mapped, '!' '¡' '|' read as letters only inside a word, apostrophes dropped, punctuation to spaces, letter runs squeezed, single-letter runs joined, then the contractions and slang below expanded: \"isn't\" -> \"is not\", \"wanna\" -> \"want to\", \"i'm\" -> \"i am\"), and phrases are matched as whole words after the same normalisation, so a phrase is written once in its expanded form. 'patterns' are slot lists expanded to every combination ('' makes a slot optional), for sentences such as 'my dad hits me'. 'phrases', 'patterns', 'contractions' and 'normalise' are detector data, exempt from the content lint; the lines and resources are linted like any player text, except that they may name the real support services (combat and sexual words such as 'violence' and 'sexual assault' are allowed there).",
